Third, we evaluate the impact of these behaviors on the users’ perceived workload and social perception in real-world experiments involving non-expert users.

The remainder of this paper is organized as follows. First, we analyze the motion parameters that influence human perception and define representative interaction behaviors. Then, we briefly summarize the predictive control framework previously developed to ensure safety, and describe its extension to implement these interaction behaviors. Finally, we present experimental results obtained with non-expert users interacting with the robot in realistic conditions.

